{
 "description": "desired.v2 §2.5, the watch: one target, the base-relative `key` of its slice, the version it `held` ({kind: put | delete, version, last_known?} or null), whether it `moves` what it expects at its own change (§2.5's MAY), and its steps -> what each does, what the target expects after each, and whether the version it holds is still last-known at the end. Computed twice by two scripts of the text's drafter that share no code, kept out of the repository, and never blessed. A step is one of: {heartbeat: {run, seq, section, members?}}, a heartbeat read by freshness.v2 §2.5's steps, its key's run (4 or 8 hexadecimal digits) and seq, and the section of the author's desired collection, {digest, live}, or null where the collection's map bit is 0; members, where given, are the author's live members, each {key, version}, of which the section is core §7.5's digest (the XOR of the first 4 bytes of the sha256 of each member's key, a zero byte, its run's width bit, its run and its seq) and their count; {heartbeat: {run, seq, read: \"revision\" | \"refused\"}}, one of another revision, or one core §7.5 refuses; {heard: {kind, version}}, a version of the slice heard live and admitted; {answer: \"unchanged\" | {whole: {kind: put | delete | no_entry, version?}} | \"timeout\" | \"held\"}, the outstanding read's end: the held stamp the target sent, a snapshot (its entry then the version the target holds, none for no_entry), no reply within the timeout, or a held stamp it did not send. The target starts expecting none, with no heartbeat read and no read outstanding. expect.steps, for a heartbeat, the first that answers: revision or refused (not read: it expects none, and the sequence does not move); older (in the last read one's run, its seq not after it by core §4.3's serial order: nothing changes); then, the heartbeat read and the sequence moved, the target expecting none where it is of another run than the last read one's or its seq is not that one's plus 1 modulo 2^24: no_section (it expects none); unmoved (the section is the one it expects); outstanding (a read is outstanding); read (one conditional read, carrying the version it holds, or none). For heard: moved (it moves, it expects a section and it holds a version: the old member's value XORed out where it held a put, the new one's XORed in for a put, the live count following) or kept. For an answer: unchanged (it expects the section of the heartbeat that made it read where it still holds the version it sent, else none; that version is no longer last-known), whole (it expects none), no_answer (nothing changes). expect.expects is what it expects after each step, {digest, live} or null. expect.last_known is true when the version it holds at the end came from an archive and no answer or sample of its author's carried it: an unmoved section never confirms.",
